# Ionic-ready frontend (later, not now)

Do not add Ionic or Capacitor yet. Keep the Vite React web app, but choose patterns that wrap cleanly later.

- **Pages stay self-contained.** One screen per route; logic in hooks. App chrome (header + left menu) lives in `AppLayout`, not in each page.
- **Navigation:** keep `react-router-dom`. Prefer `Link` / `useNavigate` over `window.location` (except a last-resort auth bounce). The left menu is a split pane on wide screens and an overlay drawer on small ones — that maps to Ionic `IonSplitPane` + `IonMenu`.
- **API:** keep `fetch` behind `api.js`. Do not scatter absolute localhost URLs. A configurable base URL will be needed for native later.
- **Dialogs:** do not add new `window.prompt`, `window.confirm`, or `window.alert`. Use in-app modals/forms (existing confirms can stay until touched).
- **Pointers:** every action must work with tap, not hover-only. Hover is extra, never the only way. Accordion sections open on tap.
- **Inputs:** prefer real `<button>` / `<input>` with ~44px tap targets. File pickers and color inputs should stay isolated (Capacitor plugins later).
- **Storage:** keep token access in `api.js` (`localStorage` is fine for web; native will swap to Preferences).
- **CSS:** prefer flex/grid and CSS variables. Use `--safe-top` / `--safe-bottom` (and `viewport-fit=cover`) instead of `100vh`-only layouts; `100dvh` is the web fallback. No hover-only disclosure.
- **Do not** add PWA-only APIs, browser extensions, or desktop-only drag-and-drop as the sole path for a feature.
